                <pb facs="1220" n="1070" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1070"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6766/18.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Leishman to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-10-03"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">October 3, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Reports that the extradition of Levan Kritichian, now held by the New York
                    police commissioner, has been requested by the minister for foreign affairs.
                    States that Kritichian is charged with being implicated in the murder of Apik
                    Effendi, the rich Armenian, referred to in Vartanian correspondence, who was
                    killed for refusing to donate money to the Armenian revolutionary committee.
                    Says that Kritichian is also charged with complicity in attempted assassination
                    of the Sultan two years ago, for both of which crimes he has been condemned by
                    default by the Ottoman authorities.)</p>
            </div>
